.TH "TOC2CDT" "1" "2026-11-15" "" "CDRDAO"

.SH "NAME"
toc2cdt \- writes the CD-TEXT data of a
.I cdrdao(1)
TOC file as a raw CD-TEXT pack file

.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B toc2cdt
.RB [\| \-v
.IR verbosity_level \|]
.RB [\| \-H \|]
.I input_toc_file
.RI [\| output_cdt_file \|]
.PP
.B toc2cdt
.RB { \-V | \-h }

.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.B toc2cdt
encodes the CD-TEXT data of a TOC file of
.I cdrdao(1)
into the 18 byte CD-TEXT packs that are written into the lead-in of a CD,
including the size information packs and the CRCs, and writes them to a file.
All languages, pack types and character encodings supported by the TOC file
format are encoded.

The output file contains the packs without any header or trailer. This is the
format expected by the CUE sheet
.B CDTEXTFILE
statement and used for the CD-TEXT file of a DDP image, so the output can be
used together with a CUE sheet (for example one created with
.IR toc2cue(1) )
to pass detailed CD-TEXT data to other tools.

If
.I output_cdt_file
is omitted, the name of the TOC file with its extension replaced by
.B .cdt
is used.

.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
.BI "\-v " verbosity_level
Sets the verbosity level (default 1). Level 0 only shows errors.
.TP
.B \-H
Prepends the 4 byte header returned by the MMC READ TOC/PMA/ATIP command
(2 bytes big-endian data length, 2 reserved bytes), which some tools expect.
.TP
.B \-V
Prints the version of toc2cdt.
.TP
.B \-h
Prints a usage summary.

.SH "EXIT STATUS"
0 on success; 1 if the TOC file cannot be read, contains no CD-TEXT data,
has more CD-TEXT data than fits in a block, or the output cannot be written.

.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IR cdrdao(1) ,
.I toc2cue(1)

.SH "AUTHOR"
.B toc2cdt
is part of
.I cdrdao(1).
